    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a2">

                <pb facs="0192" n="88" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg88"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 243.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hosmer to Mr. Souza</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 25,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Señor <hi rendition="#small-caps">Don F. Souza</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Agente Consular de los E. E. U. U. del Norte,
                        Retalhulen, Guatemala:</hi></p>
                <p>United States minister absent. I think Guatemalan Government has right to search
                    foreign vessels in her own waters for persons suspected of hostility to her
                    during time of war and to arrest them. You may communicate this opinion to the
                    commandant.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James R. Hosmer</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
